From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "D.R.racer" <drracer@seznam.cz>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 12:10:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] media: cedrus: h264 encoder: export per-MB information
 as a control

On P-frames the A20 VE writes one 64-bit record per macroblock: the MB
mode and its motion vectors (integer part plus a quarter-pel remainder
per 8x8 quadrant). Motion detection can use them instead of analysing
the pictures on the CPU.

Export them through a read-only U32 array control that, like
V4L2_CID_MPEG_VIDEO_AVERAGE_QP, applies to the last dequeued CAPTURE
buffer: a header (magic/version, valid flag, buffer sequence, MB grid)
followed by the records in raster order. A boolean control enables the
copy, which costs nothing when off.

Jobs complete ahead of the dequeue and the next job overwrites the MV
buffer, so job_finish copies the records into a per-CAPTURE-buffer image
and buf_finish publishes that image when the buffer is dequeued. The
images are sized from the picture format at buffer allocation: the
encoder refuses format changes while buffers are allocated, and
job_finish checks the capacity anyway.

The array follows the picture format (at open, on S_FMT) and is cleared
at every stream start, so a header from a previous session, whose
sequence numbers restarted at 0, cannot match a new buffer.

The control IDs come from a new range, V4L2_CID_USER_CEDRUS_BASE; the
layout is documented in uapi/cedrus-enc.h.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
